Record of modifications (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b))
----------------------------------------------------------

The following changes were made by NPCI relative to the upstream Grok Build
project. Each is a factual description of the state of this repository.

  1. Renaming and rebranding. Crates, binaries, environment variables and
     user-facing strings were renamed from the upstream `grok` / `xai-*` /
     `XAI_*` / `GROK_*` naming to `ainxt` / `ainxt-*` / `AINXT_*`. This
     repository contains 81 `ainxt-*` crates and reads approximately 430
     distinct `AINXT_*` environment variables. The binary is `ainxt`; user
     state is stored under `~/.ainxt/`.

  2. Gateway authentication. Bearer-token sign-in against a self-hosted gateway
     was added (`ainxt login`, `~/.ainxt/credentials.json`, `AINXT_TOKEN`,
     `AINXT_DEPLOYMENT_KEY`), including email/password and device-code flows
     against `/ainxt/v1/api/auth/*`.

  3. Model catalogue. Bundled and default model definitions were removed. The
     catalogue is obtained from a gateway the operator configures, or from
     `[model.*]` entries in `~/.ainxt/config.toml`. An unconfigured build starts
     with no models and reports that condition rather than selecting one.

  4. Compiled-in endpoints removed. Every compiled endpoint and UI URL default
     was emptied: 3 backend endpoint constants and 7 `URL_*` constants now ship
     as empty strings, and the asset host uses the reserved `.invalid` TLD.
     There is no default gateway, OAuth issuer, update origin or asset server in
     this build. Configuration is supplied at runtime through `AINXT_*`
     environment variables. The reasoning is recorded in
     `crates/codegen/ainxt-env/src/lib.rs`.

  5. Removals. The runtime TLS-verification bypass present upstream was removed;
     all three former call sites record its removal. Three upstream user-guide
     chapters were not carried over (see "Documentation" below).

  6. Additions. `setup.sh`, `env.example` and `INSTALL.md` were added. The
     platform installer scripts were changed to resolve releases from this
     repository's own GitHub Releases, with no third-party fallback download
     origin.

This list is maintained in this file. It is a summary and not a substitute for
the commit history; where the two differ, the history governs.

Documentation
-------------

The user guide under `crates/codegen/ainxt-pager/docs/user-guide/` is derived
from the upstream guide at `crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager/docs/user-guide/` in
the Grok Build project. Chapters 01-24 correspond to upstream chapters of the
same number and filename, adapted for the renaming and behavioural changes
recorded above. Three upstream chapters are not present in this fork:
`25-status-line.md`, `26-config-reference.md` and `27-grok-clone.md`.

Upstream's own documentation at https://docs.x.ai/build/overview remains the
reference for behaviour this fork did not change.

